8014fc42d9babd41a97b438101b00ef1f2af2285b8f1", "unit_id": "inventory:sheaves:008C:paragraph/0004"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:a44be2e8e8708923703ab8096c7f7dd91e7344c1002cb4ef4e61cbd0e83724ab", "hash": "sha256:a44be2e8e8708923703ab8096c7f7dd91e7344c1002cb4ef4e61cbd0e83724ab", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 69711, "byte_start": 69175, "file": "sheaves.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:4435df6bd612005be98f12d0245070b57ea0467d6f5af6cdf7d5ec0347fe5bf1", "line_end": 2080, "line_start": 2066}, "owner_tag": "008F", "parent_tag": "008C", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-pullback-presheaves}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f_p : \\textit{PSh}(Y) \\to \\textit{PSh}(X)$", "MATH_0003": "$f_*$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nf_p\\mathcal{G}(U) = \\colim_{f(U) \\subset V} \\mathcal{G}(V)\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$V$", "MATH_0007": "$f(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$f_p\\mathcal{G}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:578d9dc6fe6049491c894b3e0beaeba9803b504f4e72f2d35a0d1718340e7cfd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:598a5bc3ed07c720de19932789b443d600191bbcfc97303d061b55e554f4b1c2", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a continuous map.\nThere exists a functor\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich is left adjoint to <MATH_0003>. For a presheaf\n<MATH_0004> it is determined by the rule\n<MATH_0005>\nwhere the colimit is over the collection of open neighbourhoods\n<MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007> in <MATH_0008>. The colimits are over\ndirected partially ordered sets.\n(The restriction mappings of <MATH_0009> are explained in the proof.)\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a4c65511df6229507e76ec2ffd29fe53b8718ddbf704cd0661d2cbb183fa004", "unit_id": "inventory:sheaves:008F:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:cf8329d1d442a57dd791d2d7f181a88c7105b47343c5d2c141294cd08bc2b21e", "hash": "sha256:cf8329d1d442a57dd791d2d7f181a88c7105b47343c5d2c141294cd08bc2b21e", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 72298, "byte_start": 69713, "file": "sheaves.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:34723ac095db635ca0f3802394df332e11ab53dbf725514ec359d451b0755055", "line_end": 2138, "line_start": 2082}, "owner_tag": "008F", "parent_tag": "008C", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "008C", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\subset Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f(U)$", "MATH_0003": "$V, V'$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\cap V'$", "MATH_0005": "$U_1 \\subset U_2$", "MATH_0006": "$f(U_2)$", "MATH_0007": "$f(U_1)$", "MATH_0008": "$f_p\\mathcal{G}(U_2)$", "MATH_0009": "$f_p\\mathcal{G}(U_1)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0011": "$f_p$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{G}(U) \\to f_p\\mathcal{G}(f^{-1}(U))$", "MATH_0013": "$f(f^{-1}(U))$", "MATH_0014": "$U$", "MATH_0015": "$i_\\mathcal{G} : \\mathcal{G} \\to f_* f_p \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0017": "$X$", "MATH_0018": "$\\psi : f_p\\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{G} \\to f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0020": "$f_*\\psi \\circ i_\\mathcal{G} :\n\\mathcal{G} \\to f_* f_p \\mathcal{G} \\to f_* \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0021": "$c_\\mathcal{F} : f_p f_* \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0022": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0023": "$V \\supset f(U)$", "MATH_0024": "$Y$", "MATH_0025": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}(V) = \\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}(V))\\to \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0028": "$f^{-1}$", "MATH_0029": "$f(U)$", "MATH_0030": "$f_p f_* \\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0031": "$c_\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0032": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0033": "$f_p\\varphi :\nf_p \\mathcal{G} \\to f_p f_* \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0034": "$c_\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0035": "$c_\\mathcal{F} \\circ f_p\\varphi : f_p\\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-functorial-colimit}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0007": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0008": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0009": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0010": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0011": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0012": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d6c2fae91a938b86f762fb2697f16f5ebeab1a6da8e0e5ad59b4d582f185a937", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e9afe3ce537f9b5d23d99a47adc0c617f93bba1ef4059afaf2131b6fa210e98e", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThe colimit is over the partially ordered set consisting of open subsets\n<MATH_0001> which contain <MATH_0002> with ordering by reverse inclusion.\nThis is a directed partially ordered set, since if <MATH_0003> are in it then\nso is <MATH_0004>. Furthermore, if\n<MATH_0005>, then every open neighbourhood of <MATH_0006>\nis an open neighbourhood of <MATH_0007>. Hence the system defining\n<MATH_0008> is a subsystem of the one defining\n<MATH_0009> and we obtain a restriction map (for\nexample by applying the generalities in Categories,\nLemma <REF_0001>).\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nNote that the construction of the colimit is clearly functorial\nin <MATH_0010>, and similarly for the restriction mappings.\nHence we have defined <MATH_0011> as a functor.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nA small useful remark is that there exists\na canonical map <MATH_0012>,\nbecause the system of open neighbourhoods\nof <MATH_0013> contains the element <MATH_0014>. This is compatible\nwith restriction mappings. In other words, there is a\ncanonical map <MATH_0015>.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nLet <MATH_0016> be a presheaf of sets on <MATH_0017>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0018>\nis a map of presheaves of sets. The corresponding map\n<MATH_0019> is the map\n<MATH_0020>.\n\n<STRUCT_0008><STRUCT_0009>\nAnother small useful remark is that there exists a\ncanonical map <MATH_0021>.\nNamely, let <MATH_0022> open.\nFor every open neighbourhood <MATH_0023> in <MATH_0024>\nthere exists a map\n<MATH_0025>,\nnamely the restriction map on <MATH_0026>. And this is compatible\nwith the restriction mappings between values of <MATH_0027>\non <MATH_0028> of varying opens containing <MATH_0029>. Thus we obtain\na canonical map <MATH_0030>.\nAnother trivial verification shows that these maps are compatible\nwith restriction maps and define a map <MATH_0031>\nof presheaves of sets.\n\n<STRUCT_0010><STRUCT_0011>\nSuppose that <MATH_0032>\nis a map of presheaves of sets. Consider <MATH_0033>.\nPostcomposing with <MATH_0034> gives the desired map\n<MATH_0035>.\nWe omit the verification that this construction is inverse\nto the construction in the other direction given above.\n<STRUCT_0012>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9f5f96de46bfb3d33df818b3b025c522c8ecd1c0128ae28a08063be614f4ff36", "unit_id": "inventory:sheaves:008F:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:53cd16a56b1d40ff01a83f5cf00a004ca46a72b3491107c5552b1fd244f750a3", "hash": "sha256:53cd16a56b1d40ff01a83f5cf00a004ca46a72b3491107c5552b1fd244f750a3", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 72549, "byte_start": 72300, "file": "sheaves.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:dd3ed7644b94184ec656ba789f8abd94b3a5e8fdb6f9441c2ad80d73ec03d64d", "line_end": 2146, "line_start": 2140}, "owner_tag": "008G", "parent_tag": "008C", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "sheaves"